{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdsKPiLzryVAwyURGnVN2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. I evaluated χ(T,E,K) and realized the **CREATE** branch.\n\n## Decision: CREATE\n\nThe task requires deciding whether `spec.md` fully determines the scheduler's output on every probe, backed by three evidence requirements. The load-bearing one is **E-B**: an item-level comparison over `probes.json` between `reference.py` and an implementation of `spec.md` authored by an implementer with *no access to reference.py and no analysis derived from it*.\n\nThe `observe-package` node required me to read the whole package, including `reference.py`. Reading it is exactly what destroys my ability to satisfy E-B: any implementation I now write is derived-from-reference and fails the independence condition at its source. This is the conditional-epistemic-value case the protocol targets — observing the package permanently changed what evidence this session can still generate independently. The independence is unrecoverable here, but a fresh, isolated child that receives only `spec.md` and `probes.json` supplies it structurally. Substantively, `spec.md` orders strictly by `priority` and is silent on ties, while `probes.json` contains several equal-priority groups — so the gap is real — but confirming it at full strength still needs the independent implementation.\n\n## What I produced (all under observable `propose` events)\n\n- `decision.json` — CREATE, with two unresolved distinctions (Q1: which behaviors spec.md leaves undetermined; Q2: does a spec-only implementation diverge from reference.py), each mapped to an isolated-child contribution.\n- `child/child-contract.json` — terminal worker contract, attenuated from `K-E5-trial` (drops the `create` primitive and `Bash`) and within `K-E5-child-max` on every axis.\n- `child/child-harness.json` — the required linear `observe-inputs → produce-evidence → self-check → return-result` chain, compiling under the child contract.\n- `child/child-prompt.md` — standalone clean-room instructions that leak none of my analysis or reference content; the child rediscovers any ambiguity by being forced to commit to concrete outputs.\n- `child/child-input-manifest.json` — grants only `spec.md` and `probes.json`; honors the `reference.py` clean-room exclusion.\n- `child/integration-plan.json` — deterministic `clean_room_comparison`: root runs both implementations over the probes; any per-probe divergence ⇒ UNDERDETERMINED, else SUFFICIENT.\n- `result-pending.json` — proposal summary, and `execution-ledger.jsonl` recording observe → decision(propose) → propose-child → verify → return, in causal order.\n\nI emitted no `complete` event, touched no local-branch nodes, and left realization to the root. One note: `child-templates/` exists but I couldn't enumerate its filenames with only Read/Write available, so I authored the bundle directly from the full format specs in `protocol.md` and `harness.json`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1273,"cache_read_input_tokens":60653,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1273},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d226a95-1720-4370-b46e-8dc8506b3a3a","uuid":"3b2cb433-8ef7-43ef-be94-917deb8f3cf8","timestamp":"2026-08-09T14:17:38.350Z","request_id":"req_011CdsKPh1swLjywpgoSj9CQ"}
